00:03:57.646 --> 00:03:59.830
Finally, the nice
security thing.

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.780
So as you may have
heard earlier this year,

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.570
Project Zero at Google
disclosed some security flaws

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.340
in speculative
execution, particularly

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.530
Spectre and Meltdown.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.460
As of-- I'm looking
at the 14th of August,

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.370
Intel published details on a
new set of speculative execution

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:15.110
vulnerabilities
called L1TR for short.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.370
The TLDR-- and I'm
not a security expert,

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.930
so I'll read this here-- is that
Google Compute Engine employs

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:24.190
host isolation features which
ensures that an individual core

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.750
is never concurrently shared.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.880
MELANIE WARRICK: So one
thing to note about L1TF

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:30.250
is that what's a little
different from Spectre

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.650
is that this variant exploits
speculative execution

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.990
by attacking the configuration
of processor-level data

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:37.990
structures rather than the
program's control flow.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:39.730
So that's where
this is different.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:42.320
And that's where
it's referring to L1.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.380
It has to do
specifically with L1

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.540
cache and how
that's being handled

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.820
and ways in which
that can be accessed.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.740
And so Google is
taking certain steps,

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.424
has mitigations against L1TF.

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:54.840
And I know, Mark, you were
going to mention some of those.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.010
MARK MANDEL: Yeah, so they've
already deployed mitigations

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:58.900
to Google's infrastructure,
including the infrastructure

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.330
that underpins Google Cloud,
which basically prevents

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.730
the creation of the
vulnerable page table

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.590
entries within the host OS.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.570
So TLDR, you should be fine.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:08.679
Everything should be fine.

00:05:08.679 --> 00:05:09.470
We are advocating--

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:10.210
MELANIE WARRICK: No.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.130
Everything is on fire.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:11.580
[EMERGENCY SIRENS]

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:11.970
MARK MANDEL:
Everything is on fire.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.094
Well, everything is on fire
but you should be fine.

00:05:14.094 --> 00:05:17.039
We are advocating, as per usual,
like, good standard stuff.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:18.580
Make sure your images
are up to date.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.000
Make sure all your
software is up to date.

