00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.150
App Engine has always been
about a really strong developer

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.990
experience or security built
in the serverless model,

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.790
and we're here to
talk about that today.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:32.420
MELANIE WARRICK: Nice.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.795
MARK MANDEL: Yeah, so people
who aren't familiar with App

00:06:34.795 --> 00:06:36.000
Engine, give us the pitch.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.125
STEREN GIANNINI: All right.

00:06:37.125 --> 00:06:40.190
App Engine is a fully managed
serverless application

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:40.975
platform.

00:06:40.975 --> 00:06:43.790
It was really serverless
before it was cool.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:47.360
So it scales to zero,
you pay for what you use,

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.040
and there is no
server management.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.490
We entirely abstract the
infrastructure from you.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.050
Deployments are source-based.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:57.350
So what you give is your
application source code.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.370
Then it deploys fast.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.200
There's a built pipeline.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.221
There's a built-in versioning
and traffic-splitting features.

00:07:04.221 --> 00:07:05.220
STEWART REICHLING: Yeah.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:06.936
So it's often just
been about, you

00:07:06.936 --> 00:07:08.810
are a developer who
wants to write your code.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.880
You don't want to have
to think about setting up

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.817
and wiring and the complicated
things around scaling.

00:07:13.817 --> 00:07:16.400
App Engine's really supposed to
give you that simple developer

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.550
experience, plus things like
a pay-per-use billing model

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:20.791
and good scaling.

00:07:20.791 --> 00:07:22.790
MELANIE WARRICK: And we
use App Engine for our--

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:23.190
MARK MANDEL: Podcast.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:23.840
MELANIE WARRICK: --website.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:24.530
